  ],
  "text": "In nineteen forty seven a moth got stuck in a relay. They taped it into the logbook. The note beside it reads first actual case of bug being found. The word was already in use. The joke was finding a literal one. But the expensive bugs are not insects, and they are almost never one mistake. Mariner one was destroyed because of a single wrong character in a formula. Ariane five exploded because working code from the last rocket met a bigger number than it expected. The Therac twenty five gave massive radiation overdoses because two subsystems disagreed about state. Notice the pattern. Every part worked. The joins did not. And the biggest one mostly did not happen, because people spent years quietly fixing it first. Complexity does not cause bugs on its own. Handovers do. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
